    <ferc:StatementAboutImportantChangesDuringTheQuarterYearTextBlock id="f-262" contextRef="c-53">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p style="text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; background-color: unset; font-size: 12pt; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;1. None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class="Section_1"&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: normal"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;2. None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: normal"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: normal"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;3. None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: normal"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: normal"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;4. None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: normal"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: normal"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;5. None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: normal"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: normal"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;6. None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: normal"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: normal"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;7. None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: normal"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: normal"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;8. None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: normal"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: normal"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;9. See page 122.1 Note G - Commitments, Contingencies and Environmental Liabilities&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: normal"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: normal"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;10. None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: normal"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: normal"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;11. S&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: nowrap; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); display: inline !important; float: none"&gt;ee page 122.1 Note G - FERC Proceedings&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: normal"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: normal"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;12. During the reporting period, the following changes occurred:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: normal"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" style="width: 538.75pt; border-collapse: collapse" class="e-rte-table"&gt; 				&lt;tr style="height: 15pt"&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 3.35pt; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: bottom; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1)"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: normal"&gt; 							&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 137.05pt; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: bottom; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1)"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: normal"&gt; 							&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; text-decoration: underline"&gt;Removals:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 365.95pt; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: bottom; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1)"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: normal"&gt; 							&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 				&lt;/tr&gt; 				&lt;tr style="height: 15pt"&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 3.35pt; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: bottom; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1)"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: normal"&gt; 							&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 137.05pt; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: bottom; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1)"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: normal"&gt; 							&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 365.95pt; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: bottom; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1)"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: normal"&gt; 							&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 				&lt;/tr&gt; 				&lt;tr style="height: 15pt"&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 3.35pt; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: bottom; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1)"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: normal"&gt; 							&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 137.05pt; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: bottom; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1)"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: normal"&gt; 							&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;David W. Coker&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 365.95pt; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: bottom; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1)"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: normal"&gt; 							&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Vice President - ETT Power Optimization&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 				&lt;/tr&gt; 				&lt;tr style="height: 15pt"&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 3.35pt; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: bottom; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1)"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: normal"&gt; 							&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 137.05pt; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: bottom; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1)"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: normal"&gt; 							&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Christopher R. Curia&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 365.95pt; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: bottom; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1)"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: normal"&gt; 							&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Executive Vice President &amp;amp; Chief Human Resources Officer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 				&lt;/tr&gt; 			&lt;/table&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; line-height: normal"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; line-height: normal"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;13. Not applicable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 		&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:StatementAboutImportantChangesDuringTheQuarterYearTextBlock>
    <ferc:CapitalizationOfConstructionOverheadCostRateCommonEquityRateIndicator id="f-263" contextRef="c-53">See footnote</ferc:CapitalizationOfConstructionOverheadCostRateCommonEquityRateIndicator>
    <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="f-264" contextRef="c-53">&lt;div class="Section_1"&gt; 			&lt;div style="clear: both"&gt; 				&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: right"&gt; 					&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 				&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;/div&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-weight: bold"&gt;NOTE A - ORGANIZATION AND OPERATIONS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-weight: bold"&gt;Organization.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt; Panhandle Eastern Pipe Line Company, LP (&amp;quot;PEPL&amp;quot; and, together with its subsidiaries, &amp;quot;Panhandle&amp;quot;), is a Delaware limited partnership. Southern Union Panhandle, LLC, an indirect wholly-owned subsidiary of Energy Transfer LP (&amp;quot;Energy Transfer&amp;quot;), owns a 1% general partner interest in PEPL, and Energy Transfer indirectly owns a 99% limited partner interest in PEPL.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-weight: bold"&gt;Operations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt; PEPL is primarily engaged in the interstate transportation and storage of natural gas and, as such, is subject to the rules, regulations and accounting of the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (&amp;quot;FERC&amp;quot;). PEPL owns approximately 6,195 miles of natural gas pipeline designed to transport 2.8 billion cubic feet (&amp;quot;Bcf&amp;quot;) per day. PEPL's transmission system consists of four large diameter pipelines with bi-directional capabilities, extending approximately 1,300 miles from producing areas in the Anadarko Basin of Texas, Oklahoma and Kansas through Missouri, Illinois, Indiana, Ohio and into Michigan. PEPL contracts for over 56 Bcf of natural gas storage.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;PEPL evaluated subsequent events throu&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;gh&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)"&gt;April 16, 2026&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt; t&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;he date on which these accompanying financial statements were available to be issued. Any material subsequent events that occurred during this time have been properly recognized and/or disclosed in these financial statements.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-weight: bold"&gt;NOTE B - ESTIMATES AND SIGNIFICANT ACCOUNTING POLICIES:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-weight: bold"&gt;1.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 3.33pt; font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline"&gt;Basis of Presentation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;PEPL's financial statements have been prepared in accordance with the accounting requirements of the FERC, as set forth in the applicable Uniform System of Accounts and published accounting releases, which constitute a comprehensive basis of accounting other than accounting principles generally accepted in the United States of America (&amp;quot;GAAP&amp;quot;). The most significant differences between GAAP and the financial statements presented herein are: (1) subsidiaries are reflected on the equity method whereas GAAP requires that all majority-owned subsidiaries be consolidated, (2) classification of certain accounts on the balance sheet, statement of income and the statement of cash flows, (3) certain assets and liabilities from the regulated ratemaking process are recorded that would not be recorded under GAAP for non-regulated entities, (4) classification of certain purchase accounting-related impacts from the acquisition by Energy Transfer on March 26, 2012 including purchase cost allocations that are not reflected in the financial statements presented herein in the same accounts as in GAAP based statements, and (5) current vs non-current classification of intercompany loans and advances, which may be different for GAAP purposes. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;The merger transaction between Southern Union Company (&amp;quot;SUG&amp;quot;), the previous indirect owner of PEPL, and Energy Transfer on March 26, 2012 (&amp;quot;Energy Transfer Merger&amp;quot;) was accounted for by Energy Transfer using business combination accounting. Under this method, the purchase price paid by the acquirer is allocated to the assets acquired and liabilities assumed as of the acquisition date based on their fair value. By the application of &amp;quot;push-down&amp;quot; accounting, PEPL's assets, liabilities and partners' capital were accordingly adjusted to fair value on March 26, 2012. Determining the fair value of certain assets and liabilities assumed is judgmental in nature and often involves the use of significant estimates and assumptions. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;The excess purchase cost amounts corresponding to the purchase accounting adjustments to utility plant have been reflected in Gas plant acquisition adjustments, Account 114. The amortization of these amounts is reflected in Miscellaneous amortization&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-style: italic"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt; Account 425, and Accumulated provision for amortization of gas plant acquisition adjustments, Account 115. To the extent purchase accounting balances relate to PEPL's subsidiaries, these are recorded in Investment in subsidiary companies, Account 123.1, and the related subsidiaries' income is recorded in Equity in earnings of subsidiary companies, Account 418.1.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-weight: bold"&gt;2.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 3.33pt; font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline"&gt;Use of Estimates &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;The preparation of financial statements requires management to make estimates and assumptions that affect the reported amounts of assets and liabilities and the accrual for and disclosure of contingent assets and liabilities at the date of the financial statements and reported amounts of revenues and expenses during the reporting period. Although these estimates are based on management's available knowledge of current and expected future events, actual results could differ from those estimates.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-indent: -18pt"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-weight: bold"&gt;3.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 3.33pt; font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline"&gt;Cash and Cash Equivalents&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Panhandle has a cash management agreement with Energy Transfer which authorizes Energy Transfer or its designated affiliate to provide cash management services to Panhandle. At the close of each business day, the agreement allows for Panhandle to transfer funds in excess of general operating purposes to Energy Transfer or if Panhandle has insufficient funds to meet its general operating purposes, Energy Transfer will transfer all funds necessary to Panhandle.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-weight: bold"&gt;4.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 3.33pt; font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline"&gt;Plant Materials and Operating Supplies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 58.5pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Plant materials and operating supplies are carried at the lower of weighted average cost or net realizable value. Materials transferred out of warehouses are priced at weighted average cost.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-weight: bold"&gt;5.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 3.33pt; font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline"&gt;Gas Stored Underground - Current&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 58.5pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Gas held and used for current operations is recorded to Gas stored underground - Current, Account 164.1, using the inventory method valued at weighted average cost.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-indent: -18pt"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-weight: bold"&gt;6.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 3.33pt; font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline"&gt;Natural Gas Imbalances&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Natural gas imbalances occur as a result of differences in volumes of natural gas received and delivered. Natural gas imbalance in-kind receivables and payables are valued at weighted average cost. Volume imbalances are generally settled in cash pursuant to PEPL's tariff with no impact on revenues.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-weight: bold"&gt;7.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 3.33pt; font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline"&gt;System Balancing Gas&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Gas held for operations and not expected to be used during the next twelve months is recorded to System balancing gas, Account 117.2, using the inventory method valued at weighted average cost.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-weight: bold"&gt;8.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 3.33pt; font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline"&gt;Fuel Tracker&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;The fuel tracker is the cumulative balance owed to PEPL by its customers or owed by PEPL to its customers for gas used in the operation of its system. The fuel gas reimbursement percentages are based on specified percentages pursuant to PEPL's tariff in order to provide fuel to cover gas used in the operation of its system. The net difference between the fuel reimbursement percentage received and gas used in the operation of its system is valued at the weighted average cost and recorded in Other regulatory assets, Account 182.3, or Other regulatory liabilities, Account 254, as applicable. Semi-annually, in April and November, the fuel gas reimbursement will be adjusted pursuant to the tariff. The fuel reimbursement is in-kind and non-discountable. As of December 31, 2025 and 2024, PEPL's fuel tracker has a balance of $6.7 million and $1.0 million, respectively, in Other regulatory assets, Account 182.3.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-weight: bold"&gt;9.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 3.33pt; font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline"&gt;Utility Plant&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-style: italic; text-decoration: underline"&gt;Additions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-weight: bold; font-style: italic"&gt;. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Ongoing additions of utility plant are stated at original cost. PEPL capitalizes all construction-related direct labor and material costs, as well as indirect construction costs. Such indirect construction costs primarily include labor and related costs of departments associated with supporting construction activities and allowance for funds used during construction. The indirect capitalized labor and related costs are largely based upon results of periodic time studies or management reviews of time allocations, which provide an estimate of time spent supporting construction projects. The cost of replacements and betterments that extend the useful life of utility plant is also capitalized. The cost of repairs and replacements of minor utility plant items is charged to expense as incurred. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-style: italic; text-decoration: underline"&gt;Retirements&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-style: italic"&gt;. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;When ordinary retirements of utility plant occur, the original cost plus cost of removal less salvage value is removed by a charge to accumulated depreciation and amortization, with no gain or loss recorded. When entire regulated operating units of utility plant are sold, the original cost and related accumulated depreciation and amortization accounts are removed, with any resulting gain or loss recorded in the statement of income.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-style: italic; text-decoration: underline"&gt;Depreciation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-weight: bold; font-style: italic"&gt;.&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: Roboto, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, GeezaPro, &amp;quot;DejaVu Serif&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-style: italic"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: Roboto, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, GeezaPro, &amp;quot;DejaVu Serif&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;P&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;EPL computed depreciation expense under the composite method using FERC-approved depreciation rates. For general and intangible plant, PEPL computed depreciation expense under the straight-line method using FERC-approved depreciation rates. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Amortization related to the Gas plant acquisition adjustments, Account 114, is computed using the straight-line method over the average remaining life of the related asset and included in Miscellaneous amortization&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-style: italic"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt; Account 425. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-style: italic; text-decoration: underline"&gt;Allowance for Funds Used During Construction (&amp;quot;AFUDC&amp;quot;)&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;PEPL capitalizes the cost of funds used during construction for capital projects. The rates used by PEPL are calculated pursuant to FERC rules, which include an allowance for the cost of debt and equity funds. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-weight: bold"&gt;10.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 3.33pt; font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline"&gt;Asset Retirement Obligation (&amp;quot;ARO&amp;quot;) &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Legal obligations associated with the retirement of long-lived assets are recorded at fair value at the time the obligations are incurred, if a reasonable estimate of fair value can be made. Present value techniques are used which reflect assumptions such as removal and remediation costs, inflation, and profit margins that third parties would demand to settle the amount of the future obligation. PEPL did not include a market risk premium for unforeseeable circumstances in its fair value estimates because such a premium could not be reasonably estimated. Upon initial recognition of the liability, costs are capitalized as part of the long-lived asset and depreciated over the useful life of the related asset. The liability is accreted to its present value each period with accretion being recorded to operating expense or regulatory asset, as applicable, with a corresponding increase in the carrying amount of the liability. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-weight: bold"&gt;11.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 3.33pt; font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline"&gt;Related Party Transactions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Related party transactions primarily include revenues earned from and payments for services provided by Energy Transfer and its subsidiaries, including underground storage services provided by Pan Gas Storage LLC (&amp;quot;Pan Gas&amp;quot;), a direct wholly-owned subsidiary of PEPL. Transactions are generally allocated based on relevant criteria, including time spent, utility plant, gross margin, salaries, or other appropriate methods. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-weight: bold"&gt;12.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 3.33pt; font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline"&gt;Environmental Expenditures&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Environmental expenditures that relate to an existing condition caused by past operations that do not contribute to current or future revenue generation are expensed. Environmental expenditures relating to current or future revenues are expensed or capitalized as appropriate. Liabilities are recorded when environmental assessments and/or clean-ups are probable and the costs can be reasonably estimated. Remediation obligations are not discounted because the timing of future cash flow streams is not predictable. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-weight: bold"&gt;13.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 3.33pt; font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline"&gt;Revenue Recognition &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;PEPL's revenues from transportation and storage of natural gas are based on capacity reservation charges and, to a lesser extent, commodity usage charges. Reservation revenues, recognized monthly, are based on contracted rates and capacity reserved by the customers. Revenues from commodity usage charges, also recognized monthly, are based on the volumes received from or delivered to the customer, based on PEPL's tariff. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; letter-spacing: -0.1pt"&gt;Revenues collected during the pendency of a rate proceeding may be required by the FERC to be refunded in the final order. PEPL establishes reserves for such potential refunds, as appropriate. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;The balances of accumulated provision for rate refunds were nil and $5.1 million as of December 31, 2025 and 2024, respectively.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-weight: bold"&gt;14.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 3.33pt; font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline"&gt;Accounts Receivable and Allowance for Expected Credit Losses&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;PEPL has a large number of customers in the energy segment that may impact PEPL's overall exposure to credit risk, either positively or negatively, in that the customers may be similarly affected by changes in economic or other conditions. PEPL manages credit risk to mitigate credit losses and exposure to uncollectible trade receivables. Prospective and existing customers are reviewed regularly for creditworthiness based upon pre-established standards consistent with FERC filed tariffs to manage credit risk within approved tolerances. Customers that do not meet minimum credit standards are required to provide additional credit support in the form of a letter of credit, prepayment, or other forms of security.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;PEPL establishes an allowance for expected credit losses on trade receivables based on the expected ultimate recovery of these receivables and considers many factors including historical customer collection experience, general and specific economic trends, and known specific issues related to individual customers, sectors, and transactions that might impact collectability. Changes in the allowance are recorded as a component of operating expenses; reductions in the allowance are recorded when receivables are subsequently collected or written-off. Past-due receivable balances are written-off when PEPL's efforts have been unsuccessful in collecting the amount due. PEPL's allowance for expected credit losses was not material as of December 31, 2025 and 2024.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;The following table presents the relative contribution to PEPL's total transportation and storage revenues from operations that comprised at least 10% of its revenues:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 14pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" style="width: 452.15pt; border-collapse: collapse" class="e-rte-table"&gt; 				&lt;tr style="height: 14.05pt"&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 48.2pt; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: middle"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 85.35pt; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: middle"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 63.45pt; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: middle"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: center"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td colspan="3" style="width: 211.95pt; border-bottom: 1pt solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: middle"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: center"&gt; 							&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Years Ended December 31,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 				&lt;/tr&gt; 				&lt;tr style="height: 14.05pt"&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 48.2pt; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: middle"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: center"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 85.35pt; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: middle"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 63.45pt; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: middle"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 63.45pt; border-bottom: 1pt solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: middle"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: center"&gt; 							&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;2025&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 63.45pt; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: middle"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: center"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 63.45pt; border-bottom: 1pt solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: middle"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: center"&gt; 							&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;2024&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 				&lt;/tr&gt; 				&lt;tr style="height: 14.05pt"&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 48.2pt; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: middle"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: center"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 85.35pt; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: middle"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 63.45pt; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: middle"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 63.45pt; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: middle"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 63.45pt; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: middle"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 63.45pt; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: middle"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 				&lt;/tr&gt; 				&lt;tr style="height: 14.05pt"&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 48.2pt; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: middle"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin